{
  "id": "MI-HB-4138-2023",
  "scope": "state:mi",
  "title": "Enrolled House Bill No. 4138 (Public Act 19 of 2023), Weapons: firearms; license or background check for purchase of firearms; require",
  "urls": [
    "https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2023-HB-4138",
    "https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2023-2024/publicact/pdf/2023-PA-0019.pdf",
    "https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2023-2024/Journal/house/pdf/2023-HJ-03-08-022.pdf",
    "https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2023-2024/Journal/senate/pdf/2023-SJ-03-23-031.pdf"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "Sec. 2(1): (1) Except as otherwise provided in this act, a person shall not do either of the following: (a) Purchase, carry, possess, or transport a pistol in this state without first having obtained a license for the pistol as prescribed in this section. (b) Purchase a firearm that is not a pistol in this state without first having obtained a license for the firearm as prescribed in this section. This subdivision does not apply to the purchase or acquisition of a firearm that occurred before the effective date of the amendatory act that added this subdivision.\nSec. 1(1)(j): (j) \"Purchaser\" means a person who receives a firearm from another person by purchase or gift.\nSec. 2a(1)(a), (b), (d): (1) The following individuals are not required to obtain a license under section 2 to purchase, carry, possess, use, or transport a firearm: (a) An individual licensed under section 5b, except for an individual who has an emergency license issued under section 5a(4) or a receipt serving as a concealed pistol license under section 5b(9) or 5l(3). (b) A federally licensed firearms dealer. ... (d) An individual purchasing a firearm other than a pistol who has a federal national instant criminal background check performed on the individual by a federally licensed firearms dealer not more than 5 days before the purchase.\nSec. 2(3)(b): (b) The individual is 18 years of age or older or, if the firearm is a pistol and the seller is licensed under 18 USC 923, is 21 years of age or older.\nSec. 2(7): (7) This section does not apply to the purchase of firearms from wholesalers by dealers regularly engaged in the business of selling firearms at retail, or to the sale, barter, or exchange of firearms kept as relics or curios not made for modern ammunition or permanently deactivated.\nSec. 2(4): A license is void unless used within 30 days after the date it is issued.\nSec. 12(1)(f): (f) A United States citizen holding a license to carry a pistol concealed upon that individual's person issued by another state.",
